            <div xml:id="d798">

                <pb facs="1075" n="1065" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1065"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.1/3–1745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-03-17T10:00:00+07:00">March 17, 1945—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>453. To Secretary of Treasury from Adler.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>United States Army no-rate in dollars expenditures. Advances by Chinese
                        Government January 3 billion, February 4 billion, while actual disbursements
                        by Army disbursing officers were 2.6 billion in January and 2.19 billion in
                        February for engineering commission to be expended for United States Army
                        construction and operations but actual expenditures not yet known.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Fonanu Engineering Commission expenditures for United States Army between
                        5 and 6 billion. [Adler.]</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
